 ### [DashGaussian Primitive Growth Control](15744-dashgaussian-primitive-growth-control.md)
-DashGaussian Primitive Growth Control is a densification scheme that limits the final number of 3D Gaussian primitives ($N_{GS}$) by combining a threshold-based selection with a top-$k$ selection, preventing primitive explosion while maintaining reconstruction quality. It sets itself apart from standard 3D Gaussian Splatting densification by introducing a primitive budget upper-bound ($P_{fin}$) and a scheduler that dynamically constrains growth in both early low-resolution (LR) and late high-resolution (HR) optimization stages. Choose it when strict memory caps are required across multi-resolution training pipelines. [DashGaussian Primitive Growth Control](15744-dashgaussian-primitive-growth-control.md)
